A||||12||Cyberkhat||3.4 Mild performance build $$$$$??||||5||
Z||000000||Cyberkhat||11-26-2001||03:26 PM||||If I buy a decent used 3.4 how much money do ya think I would have to throw at it to get it rebuilt with a mild street buildup? I plan on removing and installing myself and doing everything else that I can myself. My costs would be the motor,parts and the machine shop. Any suggestions on what parts to use? Could I get this done on $1500? I'm just another Fiero owner that wants performance on a shoestring....||||reg||5
Z||000001||Neal||11-26-2001||07:43 PM||||for 1500 buy a crate engine install it and drive away happy, you may be able to purchase and do a stock rebuild for that $$$ but performance, hell even a clutch would break the budget.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cyberkhat||11-26-2001||08:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Neal:<BR><B>for 1500 buy a crate engine install it and drive away happy, you may be able to purchase and do a stock rebuild for that $$$ but performance, hell even a clutch would break the budget.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>That sounds like a good idea Neal.Do you have any idea how much a crate engine costs? or what the h.p. rating is stock? Thanks for the reply. Mike. <BR>||||reg||4
Z||000003||Shaun41178||11-26-2001||09:13 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cyberkhat:<BR><B> I'm just another Fiero owner that wants performance on a shoestring....</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Congratulations!  You will fit well in here with most of the other Fiero owners on here.  You can't have shoestring budget and performance in the same sentance.  Please don't be another cheapo and expect Vette performance by adding a $30 filter.<P><BR>A new 3.4 longblock will cost about $1600.  Unless you drill the starter holes and other block mods by yourself that will cost another hundred or so.  So already you are over your budget.  You can do a mild 2.8 for around $1400 or so with machine costs.  Or exchange your 2.8 for another 2.8 from autozone or some place like that.||||reg||13
Z||000004||Cyberkhat||11-26-2001||09:27 PM|||| You can't have shoestring budget and performance in the same sentance.  Please don't be another cheapo and expect Vette performance by adding a $30 filter.<P><BR>$30! Jeesh I was hoping for about $9.99! Realistically $1500 is probably too low ,eh shaun? Maybe more like $2500-$3000 to achieve enhanced performance.I'm not rich but I'll spend what I can to get what I want.<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000005||Dave Gunsul||11-27-2001||12:24 AM||||Why don't you buy a low mileage 3.4 and add some bolt on mods to it? The cost of a used engine will be far less than a new one and you can use that money to make the engine<BR>faster with some good bolt ons.<BR>Ed Parks from the Fiero Factory and/or Fiero<BR>Bob from Twin Lakes Fiero both sell used 3.4 engines and they will even sell you one that's already converted to go into a Fiero.<P>BTW a new 3.4 sells for: $1779.95 that's from my new GM catalog BTW.<BR>the specs for the 3.4 are as follows:<BR>160 HP @ 5000 RPM's<BR>194 Ib FT torque @ 2700 RPM's<BR>9.0:1 comp. ratio<BR>cam specs: 427 intake lift and 454 exh. lift<BR>duration @ .050 204 intake and 216 exh.<P><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000006||RedOktober||11-27-2001||01:57 AM||||here's the engine you need..  <A HREF="http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=598441780" TARGET=_blank>http://cgi.ebay.com/ebaymotors/aw-cgi/eBayISAPI.dll?ViewItem&item=598441780</A> <P>Here is a 3.4 V6 from a 1995 Camaro with 90K actual miles. This auction includes the engine with all accesseries, and brackets, automatic transmission, computer and wiring. The Engine & Tranny are in tip top working condition. This is a "No Reserve" auction. The high bidder wins. Don't miss this one. Winner pays actual S/I. Engine, accesseries, tranny, computer and wiring will be shipped assembled. That is, all connected. PayPal, cashiers check, or money order. Thanks. GOOD LUCK.  <P><BR>This is as cheap as u can get... Just sell the trans and recover the cost of shipping. aA couple hun for the required gaskets, and machining, etc.. and then you are ready to rock B)<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||DKOV||11-27-2001||02:16 AM||||That e-bay motor looks like a Pushrod motor...   It looks completely different from a TDC or the DOHC motors...<P>If the 215 base HP is what you are looking for, this e-bay motor is NOT the ticket.<P>DKOV -||||reg||1
Z||000008||Cyberkhat||11-27-2001||08:47 AM||||I'm not clear on what year Camaro/Firebird engines will bolt right up to the existing Fiero accessories.....Can someone help me out here..Thanks for the info so far. It really is nice to have a forum like this. Mike.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Nashco||11-27-2001||09:04 AM||||The motor that is a direct swap, shares accessories, heads, exhaust, etc. is a 93-95 Camaro 3.4 pushrod V6.  It's not much power improvement over the 2.8 stock to stock, but has a lot of the bugs worked out, has a smidge more displacement to work with, and is readily available.  The most common mod to get power out of a 3.4 is either high compression and custom fuel management or doing an entire custom turbo setup.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000010||lou_dias||11-27-2001||09:09 AM||||and don't forget a nice set of ported and polished heads and intake for that real top end power.<P>coincidentally, I have a p+p set of heads for sale  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Raydar||11-27-2001||09:22 AM||||The crate engine is rated at 160 HP as installed in an S-10, with a carb. In a Fiero it will probably make 170-180. <BR>Any 3.4 Camaro engine will work. I believe the years are 93-95. After 95, they switched to a completely different configuration 3.8. Not a good candidate for a Fiero swap.<BR>For more info on the 3.4 swap go here... <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#34" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#34</A> <P>Here's another good description of the mechanics of the swap... <A HREF="http://web2.crazydave.org:81/fiero34project/" TARGET=_blank>http://web2.crazydave.org:81/fiero34project/</A> <P>The one on e-bay is the pushrod Camaro motor. <BR>If you want a DOHC 3.4, it's more expensive to purchase, and more involved to install (you can't use the Fiero ECM), but makes tons of horsepower. 200-215 out of the box. I've heard that 300 HP is easily attained.  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 11-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Cyberkhat||11-27-2001||02:08 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Raydar:<BR><B>The crate engine is rated at 160 HP as installed in an S-10, with a carb. In a Fiero it will probably make 170-180. <BR>Any 3.4 Camaro engine will work. I believe the years are 93-95. After 95, they switched to a completely different configuration 3.8. Not a good candidate for a Fiero swap.<BR>For more info on the 3.4 swap go here... <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#34" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#34</A> <P>Here's another good description of the mechanics of the swap... <A HREF="http://web2.crazydave.org:81/fiero34project/" TARGET=_blank>http://web2.crazydave.org:81/fiero34project/</A> <P>The one on e-bay is the pushrod Camaro motor. <BR>If you want a DOHC 3.4, it's more expensive to purchase, and more involved to install (you can't use the Fiero ECM), but makes tons of horsepower. 200-215 out of the box. I've heard that 300 HP is easily attained.  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>There is some valuable information here.I feel like I'm on my way. Thanks!<BR>||||reg||3
